-- creature_template_model rows that point at a CreatureDisplayID the Classic client does not have.
-- These rows come from the retail world data. At startup the server skips each one and logs
-- "Creature (Entry: x) lists non-existing CreatureDisplayID id (y), this can crash the client.",
-- so they are never used in game. Only rows of creatures that keep at least one valid model are removed,
-- so no creature loses its look; creatures with no valid model at all are left untouched.
-- 13683 rows on 10852 creatures. Checked against CreatureDisplayInfo.db2 (1.15 client data) and hotfixes.creature_display_info.
-- Safe to run again.
